    "updated_at": "2020-05-18T10:17:15Z",
    "body": "I can confirm there is no event for this, this transition isn't covered in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#ready-states.\r\n\r\n@mightyiam have you confirmed that the state transition itself happens in some browsers, and is independent of the decrease to 2, HAVE_CURRENT_DATA? If the state transition does happen (without a dedicated event) then could you try checking for it the \"timeupdate\" event to make an example of what \"let my user know that buffering is imminent or expected some time in the future\" would look like?\r\n\r\nThe difference between HAVE_FUTURE_DATA and HAVE_ENOUGH_DATA is one of heuristics, and what I suspect is that no implementation really treats them as separate states, but rather goes directly from 2 to 4, and 4 to 2. But it's been a while since I worked on this so I'm not sure that's true any longer.",
